<Layout pageTitle="Axon-Resolution Laboratory · Methods & Validation" description="Explicit bipolar geometry, insulating-well equations, fixed identity accounting, numerical evidence and retained failures." wide compactHeader>
<div class="ax-lab ax-methods">
<SimHero kicker="Axon resolution / Methods and evidence" title="A result with a traceable denominator" intro="Physical geometry, matched interventions and numerical error are part of the result." links={[{href:'/simulations/biohybrid-axon-interface/',label:'Open laboratory'},{href:'/simulations/biohybrid-axon-interface/questions/',label:'Scientific questions'},{href:'/simulations/biohybrid-axon-interface/validation.json',label:'Full validation JSON'}]}/>
<div class="ax-boundary"><span class="ax-kicker">Model boundary</span><p><strong>{evidence.completeStage1?'Conditional Stage 1 · numerical release gates passed.':'Stage 1 development · final source verification pending.'}</strong> Explicit bipolar projecting cells, finite electrode contacts, insulating wells, anisotropic conduction and a resolved perineurium. Engineered anatomy is imposed as a hypothesis; survival, appropriate target reinnervation and human ganglion physiology are not calibrated.</p></div>

<section id="scope">
<h2>01 · Implemented experiment and release boundary</h2>
<p>The main experiment is the B3 ganglion-replacement hypothesis. Each introduced E cell owns a peripheral and a central projection, so it needs no invented excitatory synapse onto a myelinated host shaft. Its soma, two unmyelinated stems, heminodes and myelinated arms are distinct electrical structures. Every declared cell has a physical insulating well; only the selected contact pairs are driven, and every other cell remains a possible off-target response.</p>
<p>The default resolves {defaults.axonCount} cells and {defaults.channelCount} isolated channels. The 256-cell preset uses a 350 µm-radius fascicle and one contact pair. The four-cell preset uses the same equations and explicit resolution. No population screening, threshold interpolation, hidden well removal or extrapolation to a full human nerve occurs.</p>
<div class="ax-table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Stage 1 requirement</th><th>Implementation</th><th>Qualification</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>37 °C myelinated membrane</td><td>MRG double cable with independent native NEURON reference</td><td>Motor-fiber mechanisms are an explicit hypothesis when assigned to engineered bipolar cells.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Bipolar replacement geometry</td><td>Soma bands, asymmetric stems and two myelinated arms</td><td>Fixed electrical paths; biological growth and target reinnervation are not inferred.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Electrode well and aperture</td><td>Finite surface contacts and conforming tetrahedral conductor</td><td>Ideal insulating walls, ohmic fluid and a declared finite outer boundary.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Original census</td><td>Immutable H identities and separate introduced E identities</td><td>Complete resection makes strict original-host continuity zero.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Architecture-appropriate controls</td><td>Zero drive, isolated channels, regional/soma/whole-cell silencing and true no-device</td><td>Junction block is not applicable because B3 has no junction. It is never scored as passed.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Independent numerical verification</td><td>Python field assembly, native NEURON and refinement studies</td><td>{evidence.completeStage1?'The final evidence agrees with the frozen numerical source.':'Final source-stable reproduction remains a release gate.'}</td></tr>
<tr><td>Physiological diameter relation</td><td>Published cat relation compared explicitly</td><td>Unresolved discrepancy remains disclosed; numerical agreement is not physiological calibration.</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<p>Model version: <code>{STAGE1_MODEL_VERSION}</code>. Bipolar component: <code>{BIPOLAR_VERSION}</code>. The separate straight-cable benchmark retains its own settings and result meaning under <code>{CORE_VERSION}</code>. Coil/optical fields, growth, whole-nerve screening, oxygen, fabrication, interconnect, chronic change and refinement belong to later build stages.</p>
</section>

<section id="identities">
<h2>02 · Census, continuity and the win condition</h2>
<pre>Y_original =
|H_original ∩ continuous ∩ recruited ∩ exclusive ∩ mechanism-dependent|
/ |H_original|

Complete declared ganglion resection:
continuous original identities = empty
Y_original = 0 / N_original

E identities are introduced neurons.
An E output never becomes an H identity.</pre>
<p>The original-host ratio is structurally zero in this complete-resection architecture, even when an engineered output is individually recruited. That is an identity consequence of the declared operation, not a forecast of recovery. The E-output fraction uses the retained original census as its denominator and is explicitly conditional on the imposed engineered paths. Target reinnervation, survival and appropriate functional connections remain unknown.</p>
<p>The matched no-device case uses the same original census, seed, resection and absent-original-remnant assumption. It removes the implanted E cells, well walls and contacts, and has no implant drive. Its zero-source conductor has the exact zero-potential solution; its empty excitable population has zero neural current. It is not renamed as an intact nerve or a successful repair.</p>
<p>A separate viable-stump diagnostic retains explicitly disconnected native peripheral and central cable graphs. Its viability is an imposed instantaneous assumption. Because it has a different remnant state, it is not the matched no-device comparator and does not estimate biological implant benefit. The assumed intact preoperative count is also a separate context.</p>
<p>Electrical exclusivity requires a channel row with exactly one recruited E output. Shared rows retain every co-recruited identity. Conditional local-initiation evidence additionally requires loss under regional active-conductance removal and the earliest observed threshold crossings within that region. Soma-only loss is a separate necessity diagnostic. Neither threshold-crossing order nor removal-induced loss, by itself, proves the origin of depolarization.</p>
</section>

<section id="membrane">
<h2>03 · Explicit bipolar double cable</h2>
<p>The myelinated mechanisms follow the original <a href="https://modeldb.science/3810">MRG ModelDB source</a>, pinned to commit <code>{MRG_SOURCE.commit}</code>. Nodes carry fast sodium, persistent sodium, slow potassium and leak. MYSA, FLUT and STIN regions retain distinct geometry and passive membranes; periaxonal resistance and myelin capacitance/conductance form the second cable. Only published tabulated outer-fiber diameters are accepted for those arms.</p>
<pre>V_m = V_intracellular − V_periaxonal
V_periaxonal,absolute = w + φ_e

I_m = C_m dV_m/dt + I_Naf + I_Nap + I_Ks + I_leak
I_myelin = C_my d(w)/dt + G_my w

Intracellular and periaxonal axial-current balances
are advanced together by a block cable solve.
Extracellular voltage enters differences along the physical cable.</pre>
<p>The default soma diameter is {defaults.somaDiameterUm} µm, with {defaults.somaSegments} axial spherical bands. Peripheral and central stems have separately stated lengths and diameters. Each myelinated arm contains {defaults.armNodeCount} true nodes. The default morphology resolves {morphology.compartments.length} membrane compartments and {morphology.activeSiteIndices.length} active-site event locations. The soma and stems use declared fractions of MRG nodal active density; these are hypothetical parameters, not measured human SGN fits.</p>
<p>Each soma band receives an area-consistent surface-averaged extracellular potential. This remains a one-dimensional cable reduction: circumferential nonlinear membrane polarization is not resolved. The physical spherical exclusion geometry is identical when its electrical bands are refined, so the soma convergence comparison changes electrical resolution without moving a wall, contact or cell surface.</p>
<p>The current settings use {defaults.dtMs*1000} µs time steps, {defaults.passiveSegments} passive subdivisions and {defaults.stemSegments} stem subdivisions. A {defaults.equilibrationMs} ms preparation precedes the observed electrical window. Each matched conductance intervention starts from the same prepared state. No leak reversal is corrected to force rest, no voltage is clipped, and no trace is shifted or rescaled before comparison.</p>
<p>The one-band model was insufficient under the actual well field: one-to-three and three-to-five band comparisons failed. The supported resolution is selected by consecutive passing refinements under unchanged acceptance thresholds. Earlier passing isolated-cell fixtures remain historical evidence for their own geometry, not a substitute for the field-coupled soma study.</p>
<p>A passive somatic band can cross a voltage threshold because of electrotonic or imposed-field effects. The interface therefore reports “threshold crossing” and names the observed site. Regenerative activity and an anatomical mechanism cannot be inferred from that label alone.</p>
</section>

<section id="field">
<h2>04 · Physical insulating wells and anisotropic field</h2>
<pre>∇ · (Σ ∇φ) = 0 in conducting tissue and fluid
Σ_endo = diag(σ_transverse, σ_transverse, σ_longitudinal)

On an electrode patch: prescribed finite surface current density
On an insulating wall or excluded cell surface: n · Σ∇φ = 0
On the declared outer cylinder and ends: φ = 0

K_ab = Σ_elements volume × (∇N_a)ᵀ Σ (∇N_b)
K φ_k = b_source,k − b_return,k
φ(t) = Σ_k I_k(t) φ_k</pre>
<p>The mesh conforms to each cavity, side wall, end cap, annular aperture and finite contact patch. Wall and cell-interior tetrahedra are excluded from the conductor; their natural boundary condition imposes zero normal current. The endoneurium, perineurium, epineurium and surrounding conductor remain distinct regions. Perineurium thickness and resistivity are exposed inputs because their values are preparation-dependent.</p>
<p>The well cavity radius, length, wall thickness, aperture radius and contact dimensions are hypothetical physical inputs. There is no adjustable shielding factor. Contact areas are integrated from the actual mesh faces and carried into charge-density arithmetic. Cell–wall intersections, overlapping wells, singular patches, nonconducting sampling points, unbounded meshes and unsupported requests raise visible errors.</p>
<p>The local model explicitly excludes the soma and neurite envelope through the well and a declared extension around it. Farther along the projecting arms, cables are embedded in the effective bulk endoneurial tensor. The local-domain-extension study measures sensitivity to that transition. This is an explicit multiscale modeling boundary, not a claim that the individual cable surfaces are resolved over the entire fascicle length.</p>
<p>Potential is averaged over each compartment’s physical membrane sampling surface. The same linear functional defines the reciprocal recording coefficient. Refinement studies separately check radial, angular, axial and membrane-surface quadrature choices. A dense adjacent-well fixture gates every cell and neighboring-well coupling individually; a large target response cannot hide a poor off-target coefficient.</p>
<p>The imposed electrode field drives each cable independently. Membrane-generated extracellular fields are calculated for reciprocal recording but are not fed back into the membrane equations of the same cell or its neighbors. Self-consistent ephaptic coupling is absent. The dense-neighbor study verifies electrode-to-cell transfer accuracy; it does not validate an omitted cell-to-cell feedback mechanism.</p>
<p>The grounded-domain study expands both outer radius and half-length by 1.5× under the same field-refinement gate. It measures sensitivity of the stated fixture to a finite boundary. Analytic infinite-medium and layered-cylinder benchmark boundary conditions remain separate checks; they are not relabeled as a blanket proof of an infinite production domain.</p>
<h3>What the aperture resistance means</h3>
<pre>I_aperture = discrete conservative current through the annular bore
ΔV_bore = area-mean potential at inner plane − outer plane
R_bore = ΔV_bore / I_aperture

mV / µA = kΩ
Uniform-annulus comparison: R = L / (σ A)</pre>
<p>The reported bore ratio comes from the solved field and conservative cuts inside the cap. Access and near-field effects are included in the full electrode-pair solution but are not folded into that bore-only ratio. A near-zero bore current produces a null ratio rather than an unstable resistance estimate. Current leaving one end returns through the other; summing their absolute values would double-count the path.</p>
<p>The aperture sensitivity study recalculates every field and matched membrane intervention. Narrowing an aperture changes both confinement and the potential required to drive a given escape current. Neither the geometry nor a sampled potential-range ratio alone establishes single-cell recruitment.</p>
</section>

<section id="controls">
<h2>05 · Matched interventions and source-separated recordings</h2>
<div class="ax-table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Condition</th><th>Change</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Assigned isolated channel</td><td>Only the named finite source/return pair is driven.</td><td>Defines the complete channel row against every declared E cell.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Zero stimulus</td><td>Drive set to zero, with the same preparation and morphology.</td><td>Tests spontaneous activity and drift over the full observation window.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Regional silencing</td><td>Active conductances removed at the soma, both stems and proximal heminodes.</td><td>Tests local active-conductance dependence while retaining distal excitability and the field.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Soma-only silencing</td><td>Active conductances removed at every somatic band only.</td><td>Tests conditional somatic-conductance necessity, not where the field first depolarized the cell.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Whole engineered-cell silencing</td><td>All E active conductances removed; passive membranes and field retained.</td><td>Checks active-cell dependence. Loss alone cannot establish soma mediation.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Junction block</td><td>Not applicable to this projecting-neuron topology.</td><td>No invented host-shaft junction and no false passing score.</td></tr>
<tr><td>True no-device</td><td>E cells, wells, electrodes and implant drive removed; the original-remnant assumption stays matched.</td><td>Exact zero electrical solution under the fixed resection anatomy; no repair forecast.</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<p>Three same-ordinal upward crossings at consecutive distal nodes must have positive delays, segment speeds within the declared numerical diagnostic range and compatible inter-node speeds. Those gates reject obvious simultaneous field deflections. They do not prove that the same regenerative event traversed a biological axon or reached an appropriate organ. Both projecting arms are retained in the trace data.</p>
<pre>V_record,neural = Σ_i T_record,i I_outer,i
I_outer [nA] × T [mV/µA] gives recording [µV]

V_total(t) = V_imposed(t) + V_engineered(t) + V_original(t)</pre>
<p>Recordings use the current entering the volume conductor, with myelin and periaxonal bookkeeping. Internodal axolemmal current is not indiscriminately assigned to extracellular space. Source components are known forward-model terms, not an inverse reconstruction or spike-sorting result. Original-source voltage is zero in the matched replacement domain because that population is assumed absent; the separate viable-stump diagnostic is not secretly added to it.</p>
<p>Saved membrane currents and the imposed artifact use the same preceding solver-step average. Exports retain the interval start and end as well as the saved state time. Instantaneous voltages add; peak-to-peak magnitudes do not. A nonzero recorded waveform alone does not establish that an axon fired.</p>
<p>A failed zero-drive or silencing audit withholds electrical selectivity headlines. Unsupported voltage excursions stop that calculation. Parameter studies retain an explicit failure at its original sampled value and withhold threshold brackets if any required point fails. A failed point is never converted into non-recruitment.</p>
</section>

<section id="parameters">
<h2>06 · Parameter register and evidence classes</h2>
<p>Every parameter below has exactly one evidence class: experimental, mathematical, estimated or hypothetical. “Estimated” means an explicit modeling or numerical choice. “Hypothetical” means a proposed architecture or biological input. The entire fixed replacement anatomy is hypothetical, and the supported MRG equations do not convert it into a measured engineered neuron.</p>
