<section id="physiology">
<h2>Published diameter relation remains unresolved</h2>
<p>The broad class velocity bands are numerical diagnostics. They do not establish the published diameter relation. The comparison below uses 41 nodes, finer time/space resolution and monitoring locations away from initiation and sealed ends. The cited larger-cat-fiber line is 5.66 m/s per µm. No tolerance was invented after observing the discrepancy.</p>
<div class="ax-table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Outer diameter</th><th>Calculated velocity</th><th>Published cat-line value</th><th>Relative difference</th></tr></thead><tbody>{(mrg?.conductionLiteratureComparison??[]).map(c=><tr><td>{c.fiberDiameterUm} µm</td><td>{format(c.measuredVelocityMps)} m/s</td><td>{format(c.literatureLineMps)} m/s</td><td>{format(100*c.fractionalDifference)}%</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
<p>The calculated fibers are slower than the cited cat relation at both tested diameters. <a href="https://journals.physiology.org/doi/full/10.1152/jn.00353.2001">MRG Figure 8 and its physiological comparison</a> concern a particular preparation. Native-solver agreement verifies the implementation of the stated equations; it does not calibrate human ganglion physiology or erase this discrepancy.</p>
</section>

<section id="failures">
<h2>08 · Retained failures and unsupported calculations</h2>
<p>The original coarse MRG time steps and passive-section resolution, the enlarged active-node “soma,” the first field source/refinement treatment, the first bipolar time step and the one-/three-band soma approximations are retained with measured values and their corrections. A different passing model never turns an earlier failed one into a pass.</p>
{retained.map(f=><details class="ax-inspection"><summary>{f.id??f.name??f.cause??'Retained failed experiment'}</summary><pre>{JSON.stringify(f,null,2)}</pre></details>)}
<p>The early field radial-refinement discrepancy was 19.58% against the unchanged 10% gate. Correcting physical source integration and mesh refinement reduced that benchmark discrepancy; it did not change the gate. The bipolar 1.25 µs time-step comparison failed its 1 mV maximum-site RMS gate. Its finer supported time step and the five-band soma correction are numerical-resolution changes, not fitted changes to conductance density.</p>
{evidence.amplitudeProbe&&<details class="ax-inspection"><summary>Declared amplitude probe, including model-domain rejections</summary><pre>{JSON.stringify(evidence.amplitudeProbe,null,2)}</pre><p class="ax-fine">Each probe retains its morphology version. Historical one-band outcomes are not evidence for the final five-band model. An unsupported-voltage case is neither a passing result nor a non-recruited sample.</p></details>}
<p>An execution-environment reset interrupted the first implementation before its source checkpoint. Exact field and protocol sources were recovered by their retained hashes; the membrane source was reconstructed from the pinned upstream mechanism. Fresh reports verify the recovered revision. Recovery provenance and original failed measurements remain separate from newly executed evidence.</p>
</section>

<section id="reproduction">
<h2>09 · Reproduction, work limits and exports</h2>
<pre>python3 scripts/axon-interface/reproduce-stage1.py
node --test tests/axon-interface-contracts.mjs tests/axon-interface-stage1-contracts.mjs
npm run build
node scripts/verify-axon-interface-build.mjs</pre>
<p>The single reproduction entry point pins NEURON, NumPy and SciPy, builds the original native mechanism, executes the independent field and membrane references, runs the explicit well/soma studies and the full-population protocol, and records runtime hardware and before/after source hashes. A source change during execution invalidates that run. Large raw arrays are regenerated from the committed source; compact reports, acceptance files, source pins and retained failure snapshots are committed.</p>
<p>The optional <code>--verify-existing</code> mode checks current source hashes, acceptance files and the already executed reports. Its aggregate is explicitly labeled <code>verified-existing-evidence</code>; it does not claim the studies were rerun together. Use the default command above to regenerate every required numerical study and the full-population run from source.</p>
<p>Stage 1 caps include {STAGE1_BUDGET.maxCableSolves.toLocaleString('en-US')} cable solves, {STAGE1_BUDGET.maxCompartmentSteps.toLocaleString('en-US')} compartment steps and {STAGE1_BUDGET.maxSavedValues.toLocaleString('en-US')} scalar saved/temporary values. Field node, tetrahedron, sparse-matrix and estimated-memory limits are separate and published in the register. The 256-cell calculation is a substantial explicit mesh. Actual measured runtime and memory are reported with their environment; Node timings are not presented as browser performance predictions.</p>
<p>Every electrical solve runs in a Web Worker. Cancellation terminates that worker. Request identities prevent an old response from replacing a newer request. Editing controls preserves the original settings of completed and pinned results. The anatomy, membrane replay, exact-value table and 2D fallback share retained physical identities and data. Display color saturation never clips numerical voltage or feeds back into physics.</p>
<p>JSON retains normalized settings, versions, units, original and engineered identities, morphology, transfer coefficients, all interventions, matrices, source-separated recordings, study failures and limitations. CSV exports recruitment, per-site events, the cascade and sampled source time series with the completed settings. Import restores parameters for a fresh calculation; it never adopts an imported result as verified evidence. Replay is deterministic within the same runtime and model revision.</p>
</section>

<section id="limits">
<h2>10 · Standing limitations</h2>
<ul>{STAGE1_LIMITATIONS.map(text=><li>{text}</li>)}</ul>
<p>Passing these tests establishes agreement with the stated numerical equations at the stated fixtures. It does not establish an implanted organoid’s biology, a functional host-shaft junction, appropriate reinnervation, sensation quality or a device lifetime. No output is a device specification, surgical recommendation or prediction of human recovery.</p>
</section>

